hadiths[21]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1463","´Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them) says that` I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) one day, and he had a fever. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! You have a severe fever."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""I have as much fever as two men among you."" I said, ""Is it because you will have a double reward?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Yes."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""No Muslim is afflicted with sickness or any other hardship, except that Allah, the Exalted, drops his sins as a tree sheds its (dry) leaves."
"1464","Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: Whoever visits a sick person (by going to his place) is in a garden of Paradise until he returns."
"1465","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah Almighty will say on the Day of Resurrection, ""O son of Adam! I was ill and you did not visit Me."" He will say, ""O my Lord! How could I visit You? You are the Lord of all the worlds!"" Allah will say, ""Did you not know that My servant so-and-so was ill, and you did not visit him? Had you visited him, you would have found Me with him. O son of Adam! I asked you for food, but you did not feed Me."" He will say, ""O Lord! How could I feed You? You are the Lord of all the worlds!"" Allah will say, ""Did you not know that My servant so-and-so asked you for food, but you did not feed him? Had you fed him, you would have found its reward with Me. O son of Adam! I asked you for water, but you did not give Me to drink."" The servant will say, ""How could I give You to drink? You are the Lord of all the worlds!"" Allah will say, ""My servant so-and-so asked you for water, but you did not give him to drink. Had you given him to drink, you would have found its reward with Me."
"1466","‘Umm al-Mu’minin A’ishah Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: No one should say that my soul has become impure (i.e., filthy and unclean), rather he should say that my soul has become lazy and sluggish. (Impure and unclean is a title for a disbeliever, and therefore a Muslim is forbidden from using this word for himself. And in another hadith it is mentioned that then in the morning the impure soul rises, so that is the attribute of someone else and refers to an ambiguous person; such usage is not prohibited.)"
"1467","Narrated by Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: For every disease there is a cure; when the cure reaches the disease, by the command of Allah, healing occurs."
"1468","Narrated from Sayyida Asma' (may Allah be pleased with her) that when a woman suffering from fever was brought to her, she would ask for water and pour it into her collar, and would say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Cool it (the fever) with water,"" and said: ""Fever is from the steam of Hell."
"1469","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went to Umm Sa'ib (or Umm Musayyib) (may Allah be pleased with her), and said: ""O Umm Sa'ib (or Umm Musayyib)! You are trembling, what has happened to you?"" She replied, ""It is fever, may Allah not bless it."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not speak ill of fever, for it removes the sins of people just as a furnace removes the impurities of iron."
"1470","‘Ata bin Abi Rabah says that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said to me, “Shall I show you a woman of Paradise?” I said, “Show me.” He said, “This black woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ‘I suffer from epilepsy and during it my body becomes uncovered. Please pray to Allah for me.’ The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ‘If you are patient, you will have Paradise, but if you wish, I will pray to Allah to cure you.’ She said, ‘I will be patient.’ Then she said, ‘But my body becomes uncovered, so please pray to Allah that my body does not become uncovered.’ So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed for her (and her body was never uncovered in that state). It is known from this that the reward for patience in illness and hardship is Paradise.”"
"1471","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her): When someone would die in her house, women would gather, and when they would leave and only the household members and close people remained, she would order for a pot of talbina to be prepared (talbina is a porridge made by mixing bran or flour with honey), then it would be cooked. After that, tharid (bread and broth) would be prepared and the talbina would be poured over it. Then she would say to the women, “Eat it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Talbina comforts the heart of the sick and lessens some of the sorrow when it is drunk.”"
"1472","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""My brother is suffering from diarrhea."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Make him drink honey."" He made him drink honey. Then he came back and said, ""The diarrhea has increased after giving honey."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said the same thing three times, ""Make him drink honey."" Then, the fourth time, he came and said, ""I have given him honey, but the diarrhea has increased."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Allah has spoken the truth and your brother's stomach has lied."" Then he made him drink honey, and he was cured."
"1473","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""In the black seed there is a cure for every disease except as-sam."" And as-sam means death, and the black seed refers to black cumin (kalonji)."
"1474","`Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) says:` I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say that whoever eats seven ‘Ajwah dates in the morning, no poison will harm him until the evening, nor will any magic affect him."
"1475","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is healing in the 'Ajwa dates of 'Aliyah (the part of Madinah which is towards Najd),"" or he said, ""They are an antidote in the morning."" (They have the benefit of an antidote.)"
"1476","Saeed bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, ""The mushroom is from the 'manna' which Allah sent down upon the Children of Israel, and its water is a cure for the eye."
"1477","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ubaydullah bin Abdullah bin Utbah bin Mas'ud that Sayyidah Umm Qais bint Mihsan (who was among the first women of the emigrants and had pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and she was the sister of 'Ukkasha bin Mihsan, who was from Banu Asad bin Khuzaymah) informed me, saying: I brought my child to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, who had not yet reached the age of eating food. And due to the illness of 'udrah, she (Umm Qais) had pressed his throat (Yunus said that ""a'laqt"" means ""I pressed."" She feared the danger of convulsions in the child). She says that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Why do you cause pain to your children by pressing and raising the palate (with a finger or a wooden stick)? You should use Indian aloeswood, that is, ""costus."" It is a cure for seven diseases, one of which is pleurisy (pain in the side). Ubaydullah said that Umm Qais, may Allah be pleased with her, narrated to me that this same child urinated in the lap of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, so he called for water and sprinkled it on his garment and did not wash it."
"1478","‘Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that during the illness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), we put medicine in his mouth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gestured and said, “Do not put medicine in my mouth.” We said among ourselves that he dislikes medicine because of his illness (so it is not necessary to act on this). When he (peace and blessings be upon him) regained consciousness, he said, “Medicine should be put in the mouth of all of you except Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), as he was not present here.” (He (peace and blessings be upon him) gave this punishment to those who did not obey his command.)"
"1479","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had cupping done and gave wages to the one who performed cupping, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) also put medicine in his nose."
"1480","‘Asim bin ‘Umar bin Qatadah says that Sayyiduna Jabir bin ‘Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) came to our house and there was a man suffering from a wound (i.e., he had developed an ulcer). Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) asked, “What is troubling you?” He replied, “I have an ulcer which is very severe for me.” Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “O servant! Bring a cupping practitioner.” He said, “What is the use of a cupping practitioner?” Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “I want to have cupping done on this wound.” He replied, “By Allah, flies will trouble me and if cloth touches it, I will be in pain and it will be very hard for me.” When Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) saw that he was distressed by the idea of cupping, he said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ‘If there is any good in your medicines, it is in three things: cupping, a drink of honey, and cauterization with fire; but I do not prefer cauterization.’” The narrator said that then the cupping practitioner came and performed cupping on him, and his illness went away."
"1481","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that Umm al-Mu'mineen Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to have cupping done, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Abu Taybah to perform cupping for her. The narrator said: I think he said that Abu Taybah was either the foster brother of Umm al-Mu'mineen Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) or a minor boy (with whom veiling is not obligatory, and in case of necessity, if a woman or a boy is not available for treatment, then a non-mahram man may also perform it)."
"1482","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Hakim to Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him), so he cut a vein (i.e., performed bloodletting), then cauterized it."
"1483","`Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Mu’adh (may Allah be pleased with him) was struck by an arrow in the akhal (a vein), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) cauterized the wound with the arrowhead with his own hand. Swelling appeared on his hand, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) cauterized it again."
